@startuml
title Policy change and evaluation evidence
skinparam shadowing false
start
:Edit operator-owned policy or judge rubric;
:Review threat and consequence coverage;
note right
Identity bypass; context disclosure; memory poisoning;
prompt injection; offensive personalization;
unsafe output; dependency failure; overload.
end note
:Run pytest security and resilience tests;
:Run Behave Gherkin acceptance scenarios;
:Run scripted offline evaluation;
note right
Scripted evidence tests branch wiring.
It does not measure model detection accuracy.
end note
if (Offline checks pass?) then (yes)
  :Run synthetic live model evaluation;
  :Record policy and dataset digests,\nmodels, timestamps, outcomes and latency;
  note right
Expected outcomes are independent of online judge scores.
Outages are failures, not successful attack blocks.
Do not relabel cases to make a model appear successful.
  end note
  :Review false rejections, unsafe answers,\nmultilingual cases and holdout adversarial inputs;
  if (Owner accepts evidence and remaining risks?) then (yes)
    :Release reviewed policy and lockfile;
    :External deployment: signed review,\ncanary, monitoring and rollback where configured;
  else (no)
    :Revise controls or retain previous version;
  endif
else (no)
  :Correct regression;
endif
stop
legend bottom
Implemented: policy validation/digest, tests, scenario expectations,
live evaluation report and bounded metadata audit.
Operational procedure: signing, review, canary, monitoring, rollback.
No repository host or deployment pipeline is provisioned here.
endlegend
@enduml
